      "name": "review_sentiment",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.55,
      "source_groundedness": 0.95,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "A bare positive/negative/neutral sentiment flag is fairly generic and partly redundant with existing 'Overall Rating', 'Value For Money', and 'Recommended' columns, limiting new analytical leverage. However for an open-ended 'what's in these reviews' exploration it still offers a text-derived axis crossable with dominant_topic. Values are well-grounded in the sampled source text (positives correctly identified, negative seat review correctly negative)."
    },
    {
      "name": "review_length_category",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.2,
      "source_groundedness": 0.75,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Bucketed text length is a generic metadata feature that adds little analytical leverage for understanding review CONTENT; it is close to the 'raw text length' case flagged as low value. Values are broadly derivable from the text but the thresholds appear inconsistent: the row-3 review is comparably short yet the row-1 review, similar in length, is 'medium' while a clearly longer row-4 review is 'long' — buckets are plausible but somewhat arbitrary."
    }
  ],
  "analytical_usefulness": 0.62,
